=== NOTES ===
1. NO-OP PORT outcome (precedent: Phase-43/0024 telemetry, Phase-43/0029 system).
   No source-code changes made to features/automations/, useAutomations.ts, or
   useCommands.ts. Only this log file is added. Rationale documented in the
   PREFLIGHT block above.

2. Locked-policy continuation: pages access Automation extras (execution_count,
   failure_count, consecutive_failures, last_triggered_at, last_success_at,
   last_failure_at, auto_disabled, auto_disabled_reason, preset_id,
   stop_on_failure, notify_on_run, notify_on_failure, seasonal_start,
   seasonal_end) that the api/types.ts Automation type extension claims exist
   but the backend automationResponse DTO at internal/api/automation_handler_dtos.go:14-18
   currently emits ONLY the embedded models.Automation root + next_fire_time +
   conflicts. At runtime the extras are undefined and degrade gracefully via
   existing null/falsy checks (e.g. AutomationCard's `a.failure_count > 0`
   short-circuits when undefined; `a.last_triggered_at` falls through to "Never
   run"; `a.auto_disabled` hides the warning block). Reconciling the wire shape
   requires a backend prompt to extend automationResponse + repo SQL with the
   missing columns -- out of scope for a frontend-only port. Same locked-policy
   precedent as Phase-43/0023+0024+0025+0026+0027 type-source decisions.

3. SignalThreshold UX deferred: TriggerConfigurator and ConditionBuilder accept
   numeric thresholds for any signal (battery_level %, inside_temp C, speed
   m/s, etc.) without a unit suffix or pref-aware conversion. Adding per-signal
   unit display would require a signal-to-unit map keyed by SIGNAL_FIELD_OPTIONS
   plus a two-way conversion at form-submit time, expanding the prompt scope.
   Per locked-policy precedent from Phase-43/0024 (telemetry generic raw-signal
   viewers), unit semantics live in the user-selected signal NAME and the
   backend stores thresholds in the same canonical SI unit signal_log uses
   post-Phase-42, so user-typed thresholds are interpreted correctly today.

4. Page count is 10 not 9 (gate baseline says 9). The extra .tsx is the
   AutomationListPage (singular) added in Phase-45 / Prompt 32 alongside the
   existing AutomationsListPage (plural). Both co-exist; gate accepts >= 9.

5. PowerShell-7 quirks reused from Phase-43/0021..0030:
   - Resolve-Path on the log to an absolute path BEFORE any Push-Location web,
     otherwise Tee-Object loses the file under web/.github/... during BUILD.
   - .\node_modules\.bin\tsc.cmd and npm.cmd run build instead of npx tsc /
     npm run build because pwsh -File invocation triggers npm 10
     "could not determine executable to run" error.
   - Inside the audit foreach, used ${f} interpolation instead of $f: literal
     to dodge PowerShell-7 variable-scope parser bug ($f: reads as scope
     qualifier and breaks the parser).

